  "worked_solution": "The unit price of pumpkin is $$1.78/kg.$ To find the cost of  $3$ kilograms of pumpkin, we multiply:    \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1.78\\times 3 & =5.34\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Jack paid  $$5.34$ for the $3$-$\\text{kg}$ pumpkin.",
